  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EMPOWERING WOMEN AND GIRLS ON ENTREPRENEURSHIP IN MATERIAL CULTURE SKILLS IN THE KINGDOM OF ESWATINI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Sustainable Goal 1, 2015, calls for the end of poverty in all forms. According to the World Bank Report (2023), the Kingdom of Eswatini has a population of around 1.2 million, with a per capita (Gross Domestic Product) GDP of $3,958. The poverty rate in Eswatini is estimated at 58.9% (2/3 being women); it is in this vein that a project of this nature has been incepted to empower women and girls so that they may self-sustain, alleviate poverty, and enhance social cohesion in their communities. The project will impart skills in material culture.</narrative>
  </description>
